  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "A synthetic clock",
      "items": [
        "Illustrative: one tick is drawn as one second from 2026-01-01T00:00Z, so tick 60,000 shows as 16:40",
        "The ticks are computed from the offsets in cadence/calendar.go: a site is due where (now + Offset) % Every == 0",
        "TicksPerHour 2,500 and a 60,000-tick day (domain/sim/clock)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "game/cadence",
      "items": [
        "Due(now, every, off, id) and Each(...) read only the tick and the id: no saved state, so a load fires on the same ticks",
        "Each costs end/every steps a tick, never a scan of the entities",
        "Calendar() lists every site; no two Heavy whole-map passes share a tick (TestCalendarSlots)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Measured (PERF-011 ledger)",
      "items": [
        "BenchmarkTickDayRollover500 worst tick 1.6-1.7 ms down to 1.0 ms",
        "Rot, wear and pots stay whole passes on a slot: spreading them per item rebuilt the item view every tick",
        "The scheduler's Every/Offset rows (phases.go) carry the climate, rot, wear, medical, story and social-day slots"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not on the calendar",
      "items": [
        "The hand-staggered per-pawn checks (social, mind, drugs, escape, combat, skills) keep their own staggers",
        "The 120-tick heat pass also lands on the day tick; it is Light"
      ]
    }
  ]
